# Second Brain — Mandatory Memory

`second-brain/` is **authoritative external memory**. Do not skip it. Do not treat it as optional documentation.

Full protocol lives in `CLAUDE.md` and `second-brain/README.md`. This rule enforces the habit.

## Before any non-trivial task

1. Read `second-brain/Current/Current-Context.md`.
2. Open linked feature / ADR / bug / pattern notes that the task touches.
3. Prefer vault facts over asking the user to re-explain. Link with `[[Note-Name]]` — do not duplicate vault content in chat or code comments.

## After any non-trivial task

Write back before ending the turn (pick what applies; bump `updated` frontmatter):

| What happened | Where to write |
|---|---|
| Priorities / active work changed | `Current/Current-Context.md` |
| Feature shipped or spec changed | `Product/Features/FEAT-*.md` |
| Architecture decision | New ADR under `Architecture/Decisions/` (supersede, don't rewrite old) |
| Bug found or fixed | `Engineering/Bugs/BUG-*.md` |
| Non-obvious gotcha | Append `Engineering/Lessons-Learned.md` |
| Real session progress | Append today's `Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` |

## Non-negotiables

- Pure logistics (yes/no, tiny typo) may skip write-back; everything else must update the vault.
- Prefer editing an existing note over creating a new one.
- Keep YAML frontmatter (`type`, `status`, `tags`, `created`, `updated`, `related`).
- Teaching stays in chat — never dump lessons into a root `FOR_*.md`; durable project facts go in the vault.
